# Hotpress Build Program
# Transform Inkwell into Hotpress

session "You are building Hotpress, a collaborative writing platform with live output. Read HOTPRESS_ARCHITECTURE.md for the complete specification. Follow the neobrutalist design system. Use pnpm for all package operations. Zero warnings, zero errors policy."

## Phase 1: Scaffolding (Parallel)

parallel:
  agent schema:
    context: HOTPRESS_ARCHITECTURE.md
    """
    Update the database schema in /src/lib/db/schema.ts:

    1. Add writing_sessions table with all fields from architecture doc
    2. Add liveblocks_rooms table
    3. Keep users, accounts, subscriptions tables
    4. Add proper indexes on share_slug, owner_id
    5. Run pnpm db:generate to create migration
    6. Run pnpm db:migrate to apply

    Do NOT delete old tables yet (projects, documents) - we'll deprecate later.
    """

  agent liveblocks:
    context: HOTPRESS_ARCHITECTURE.md
    """
    Set up Liveblocks integration:

    1. Install: pnpm add @liveblocks/client @liveblocks/react @liveblocks/yjs
    2. Create /src/lib/liveblocks.ts with client setup and room context
    3. Create /src/app/api/liveblocks-auth/route.ts for room authentication
    4. Create Presence and Storage types

    Use environment variable LIVEBLOCKS_SECRET_KEY for auth.
    Add NEXT_PUBLIC_LIVEBLOCKS_PUBLIC_KEY for client.
    """

  agent session-lib:
    context: HOTPRESS_ARCHITECTURE.md
    """
    Create session management library:

    1. Create /src/lib/session.ts with:
       - getOrCreateSession() - cookie-based session management
       - createSession() - create new ephemeral session
       - claimSession() - link anonymous session to user
       - SESSION_COOKIE constant

    2. Create /src/lib/format-schema.ts with:
       - TypeScript types for the format config schema
       - Zod validation schema
       - Default config for each content type (book, article, thread)
       - MVP subset defaults

    Use cuid2 for session IDs.
    """

  agent api-routes:
    context: HOTPRESS_ARCHITECTURE.md
    """
    Scaffold all API routes (stubs with types, not full implementation):

    1. /src/app/api/sessions/route.ts - POST (create)
    2. /src/app/api/sessions/[id]/route.ts - GET, PATCH, DELETE
    3. /src/app/api/sessions/[id]/claim/route.ts - POST
    4. /src/app/api/sessions/[id]/share/route.ts - POST
    5. /src/app/api/sessions/[id]/format/route.ts - GET, PUT
    6. /src/app/api/sessions/[id]/generate/route.ts - POST
    7. /src/app/api/sessions/[id]/save-to-github/route.ts - POST
    8. /src/app/api/share/[slug]/route.ts - GET
    9. /src/app/api/share/[slug]/verify/route.ts - POST
    10. /src/app/api/format/presets/route.ts - GET

    Each route should have proper TypeScript types and return TODO responses.
    Use the existing api-utils.ts patterns from Inkwell.
    """

  agent components:
    context: HOTPRESS_ARCHITECTURE.md
    """
    Scaffold new component files (structure only, not full implementation):

    Editor components:
    - /src/components/editor/SessionEditor.tsx
    - /src/components/editor/CollaboratorCursors.tsx
    - /src/components/editor/PresenceAvatars.tsx
    - /src/components/editor/EditorModeToggle.tsx

    Share components:
    - /src/components/share/ShareDialog.tsx
    - /src/components/share/PasswordGate.tsx

    Format components:
    - /src/components/format/FormatPanel.tsx
    - /src/components/format/TypographySection.tsx
    - /src/components/format/ChapterSection.tsx
    - /src/components/format/PageLayoutSection.tsx
    - /src/components/format/PreviewPane.tsx

    GitHub components:
    - /src/components/github/SaveToGitHubDialog.tsx

    Each component should have proper TypeScript interface, basic structure,
    and use the neobrutalist UI components (BrutalButton, BrutalCard, etc).
    """

## Phase 2: Implementation (Ralph Wiggum Loop)

agent implementer:
  context: HOTPRESS_ARCHITECTURE.md
  loop until **all MVP features working and tests pass**:
    """
    You are implementing Hotpress. Work through these in order:

    1. SESSIONS API
       - Implement POST /api/sessions (create session, set cookie)
       - Implement GET /api/sessions/[id]
       - Implement PATCH /api/sessions/[id] (update content, title)
       - Test with curl or the app

    2. HOMEPAGE EDITOR
       - Modify /src/app/(marketing)/page.tsx to be editor-first
       - Create session on page load
       - Connect to SessionEditor component
       - Auto-save content to DB via PATCH
       - Add type selector (Book/Article/Thread dropdown)
       - Style with neobrutalist design

    3. LIVEBLOCKS REAL-TIME
       - Connect SessionEditor to Liveblocks
       - Integrate Y.js with Lexical
       - Add CollaboratorCursors component
       - Add PresenceAvatars component
       - Test with two browser windows

    4. SHARE FLOW
       - Implement share link generation
       - Create /src/app/s/[slug]/page.tsx
       - Add ShareDialog component to editor
       - Test sharing a session

    5. AUTH MODIFICATION
       - Update /src/lib/auth.ts for optional auth
       - Update /src/middleware.ts to allow anonymous access
       - Implement session claiming when user logs in
       - Keep GitHub OAuth for "Save to GitHub"

    6. GITHUB SAVE
       - Implement /api/sessions/[id]/save-to-github
       - Create SaveToGitHubDialog with repo picker
       - Commit content as markdown + hotpress.yaml
       - Update session with github_repo, github_path

    7. BASIC FORMATTING
       - Implement format API endpoints
       - Create simple FormatPanel UI
       - Typography: font dropdowns
       - Chapters: numbering, drop caps toggle
       - Page: size presets
       - Save format config to session

    8. LANDING PAGE
       - Add HowItWorks section below editor
       - Add Features section
       - Add UseCases tabs
       - Move Pricing section
       - Add FAQ section
       - Add final CTA
       - All neobrutalist styling

    9. DASHBOARD
       - Create /src/app/dashboard/page.tsx - list user's sessions
       - Create session cards with SessionCard component
       - Link to editor and format pages

    10. CLEANUP
        - Remove old /projects routes
        - Remove old /documents routes
        - Remove old auth pages (keep OAuth callback)
        - Update all imports
        - Run pnpm lint --fix
        - Run pnpm build
        - Fix any errors

    After each major step, run pnpm build to check for errors.
    Fix all errors and warnings before moving on.

    When stuck, read the error carefully, check the architecture doc,
    and try a different approach. Keep iterating until it works.
    """

## Phase 3: Polish (Parallel)

parallel:
  agent copy:
    context: HOTPRESS_ARCHITECTURE.md
    """
    Polish all copy and messaging:

    1. Update all "Inkwell" references to "Hotpress"
    2. Update page titles and meta descriptions
    3. Review and refine landing page copy per architecture doc
    4. Ensure consistent voice (direct, not corporate, Gumroad energy)
    5. Update README.md
    6. Update CLAUDE.md with new project info
    """

  agent styling:
    context: HOTPRESS_ARCHITECTURE.md
    """
    Consistency pass on neobrutalist styling:

    1. Verify all components use brutal-* UI components
    2. Check color usage (black borders, yellow accents)
    3. Verify no rounded corners > 4px
    4. Check shadow consistency (4px 4px 0 black)
    5. Test hover/active states on all buttons
    6. Mobile responsiveness check
    """

  agent tests:
    """
    Add E2E tests with Playwright:

    1. Install Playwright if not present: pnpm add -D @playwright/test
    2. Create tests for:
       - Homepage loads, editor works
       - Create session, type content, auto-saves
       - Share link generation and access
       - GitHub OAuth flow (mock or skip)
       - Format panel opens and saves
    3. Run tests: pnpm test:e2e
    4. Fix any failures
    """

## Final Verification

agent verify:
  """
  Final checks before declaring done:

  1. pnpm lint - zero warnings
  2. pnpm build - succeeds
  3. pnpm test:e2e - all pass (if tests exist)
  4. Manual test:
     - Open homepage, type, see auto-save
     - Share link, open in incognito, see content
     - Open format panel, change font, see preview
     - Login with GitHub, claim session
     - Save to GitHub (if credentials available)
  5. Check all pages render without errors
  6. Check mobile view

  Report any remaining issues.
  """
